// What has not happened yet.
//
// Plans exist only in forecasts until the journal says they happened. `axiom forecast`
// also projects what repeats in the journal by itself (the rent, the 529 and savings
// transfers), from its cadence and amount. So a plan is for what history cannot say: a
// bill that comes once a year, a trip, a bonus. A plan with a name is also a template:
// `2026-02-13 paycheck` in the journal is one occurrence of it, written in full.

/// The monthly paycheck, 8,000 USD before tax: 800 USD deferred into the 401(k), the
/// withholding, and the rest to checking. January's is written out in the journal;
/// the next ones are just its name.
plan paycheck every month on 13 from 2026-02-13 acme -> 8_000 USD
  retirement       800 USD
  taxes/federal    880 USD
  taxes/state      370 USD
  taxes/payroll    612 USD
  checking         ...

/// Fall tuition is due in mid-August. The 529 plan pays part of it directly.
every year on 08-15 from 2026-08-15 checking -> state-u 3_600 USD
every year on 08-20 from 2026-08-20 college -> state-u 1_200 USD

/// A trip in July.
every year on 07-10 from 2026-07-10 checking -> travel 2_200 USD

/// The renter's policy renews on January 1 with a higher premium.
every year on 01-01 from 2027-01-01 checking -> insurer 630 USD

/// The year-end bonus, 4_000 USD before tax. Bonuses are withheld at flat
/// supplemental rates, and 400 USD of it is deferred into the 401(k).
every year on 12-15 from 2026-12-15 acme -> 4_000 USD
  retirement       400 USD
  taxes/federal    880 USD
  taxes/state      409 USD
  taxes/payroll    306 USD
  checking         ...
